    "evidence": "At Ethereum block 26095800 (2026-10-01), canonical GHO bytecode matched the verified GhoToken and ordinary ERC-20 implementation; the EIP-1967 implementation and correct admin slots were zero. Its transfer paths contain no holder blacklist, freeze, seizure or global pause, and the external burn function burns only the caller's balance. The current Chainlink directory identifies the nine non-Ethereum deployments as BurnMint pools. The prior inherited-status rationale cited obsolete 44.3% mainnet GSM and 7.4% stataUSDT weights. The September 30 reserve review instead records 41.630945892818% unresolved mainnet GSM residual, 2.718124202359% measured stataUSDT and positive USDC dust, plus unresolved remote allocations. Unknown residual issuance is not proof of specific issuer holdings. The adverse inherited verdict is retained pending reconciliation of the opaque exposures and owner review of the greater-than-50% test; no current threshold-satisfaction claim is made.",
    "reviewer": "Sol curation pass 2026-10-01 (CurA24GHO)",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-10-01"
